 "reading_text": "Corvan Hills Water Users Group\nQuarterly Report 2027\nPrepared by\nAmara Telham\nDate\nApril 1, 2027\n1. Background\nEarly results on the complaints procedure are clear, and work will continue before the\nspring session. A total of\n399\nhouseholds took part in the hall refurbishment.\n2. Staffing\nThe records office recommends changes to the cleaning rota once the survey results are\nin.\nFurther details on the records retention process will be shared over the next two quarters.\nThe staff council continues to monitor the maintenance budget after consultation with\nresidents. Questions about the seed library should go to\nOskar Holby,\nthe program lead.\n3. Timeline\nRequests for the tree planting day must be made at least\n7\ndays in advance. Further\ndetails on the maintenance budget will be shared so that requests are handled more\nquickly.\nPage 2",
